Corrected message:

Run custom and default text-editing keys through the same code

The text tool handled a key matching a configured shortcut and a
default key pressed with extra modifiers (e.g. Shift+Left) in two
separate copies of every editing command, and the copies had drifted.
Both now run the same code:

- Backspace and Left/Right/Up/Down/Home/End bound to a shortcut that
  includes Ctrl or Shift now do the word-wise or selecting variant,
  as the default keys with those modifiers do. Before, the modifiers
  were ignored.
- Stop Editing through its shortcut no longer runs an extra text
  redraw after committing.
- Undo reached through the default-key path now redraws the text
  afterwards, as the shortcut path did.
